From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 03:33:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix admin panel showing stale customer/order/product data
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: none of the admin data pages had an explicit dynamic-
rendering directive. A dynamic route param ([id]) alone doesn't
reliably opt a page out of Next.js's caching, so pages like the
customer detail view could keep showing data from whenever they were
first rendered/cached, even after a customer updated their own phone
number or address (which I confirmed IS writing correctly to Supabase
-- this was a stale-read bug, not a broken write).

Added export const dynamic = "force-dynamic" to every admin page that
reads live data: customers list + detail, orders list + detail, and
products list + edit (same underlying risk, fixed proactively even
though only customers/orders were reported).

🤖 Generated with Claude
